4.5 Krypton (UN1056)
Krypton is an inert noble gas stored at high pressure.
Typical operating conditions:
• Typical fill pressure: 200bar to 230bar
• Typical hydrostatic test pressure: above 300bar
Estimated pressure increase:
• Approximately 200bar at 15◦C
• Approximately 225bar at 50◦C
Primary risks:
• Stored mechanical energy.
• Asphyxiation hazard.
4.6 R1234yf (UN3161)
Chemical name:
2,3,3,3-Tetrafluoropropene
R1234yf is classified as an A2L mildly flammable refrigerant.
Approximate pressures:
• 6.7bar at 20◦C
• 13bar to 14bar at 50◦C
Primary risks:
• Mild flammability.
• Pressure rise during heating.
• Hydrogen fluoride production in fire conditions.
4.7 R1234ze (UN3163)
R1234ze is an A2L mildly flammable low-pressure refrigerant.
Approximate pressures:
• 3.5bar at 20◦C
• Approximately 7bar at 50◦C
Primary risks:
• Mild flammability.
• Pressure increase during heating.
