5 Engineering Recommendations for Heated Cabinets
5.1 Recommended Maximum Cabinet Temperature
For mixed gas storage, a conservative cabinet air temperature limit is:
Tcabinet ≤ 45 ◦C
This provides margin below the standard cylinder limit of approximately 50◦C.
5.2 Recommended Protection Features
• Dual independent temperature sensors.
• Over-temperature shutdown.
• Forced-air circulation fans.
• Thermal insulation between heaters and cylinders.
• Flammable gas detection for isobutane and A2L refrigerants.
• Ventilation or pressure relief vents.
5.3 Heater Design Considerations
The heater should:
• Avoid direct radiant heating of cylinders.
• Maintain uniform air temperature.
• Use low surface temperature elements where possible.
• Prevent local cylinder wall temperatures from exceeding safe limits.
