6 Conclusion
All listed cylinders should be treated as pressure vessels with significant stored energy. Even
inert gases become hazardous when overheated due to pressure rise.
For engineering safety:
• Maintain cabinet temperatures below 45◦C.
• Never exceed cylinder wall temperatures of 50◦C to 52◦C.
• Provide ventilation, monitoring, and over-temperature protection.
• Apply additional precautions for flammable gases and refrigerants.
